2026-05-20 12:09:19,625 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # Executive Summary
The City of Belval has issued a call for tenders to implement an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions. Our consortium, composed of specialized agents, proposes a comprehensive solution that meets the client's requirements while ensuring GDPR compliance, sovereignty of data, and high availability. Our proposed solution leverages our expertise in LLMs, RAG, and explainability to provide a powerful intelligent assistance tool for administrative activities.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires an artificial intelligence solution that can assist municipal agents in their daily missions, including searching for information, drafting letters or answers to users, and instructing files. The solution must integrate with existing systems, ensure data sovereignty, and meet regulatory requirements such as GDPR. The client also expects a high level of availability, performance, and security.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution is based on a microservices-based architecture hosted on Outscale or OVHcloud, utilizing our experience with API gateways like Kong, message brokers like Apache Kafka, and identity providers like Keycloak. We will use our knowledge of ERP/CRM connectors to integrate with existing business software and EDM systems.

For the AI components, we propose leveraging our expertise in LLMs, particularly our preferred sovereign model Mistral 7B Instruct, to develop an intelligent assistance tool that can aid agents in their administrative activities. The tool will utilize Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities to provide accurate and relevant suggestions for drafting letters or answers to users.

The proposed AI components include:

* A fine-tuned Mistral 7B model for generating text based on the administrative context
* A RAG module that integrates with our vector stores experience, such as Qdrant or Weaviate, to retrieve relevant information from a knowledge base of administrative procedures and regulations
* An explainability component using XAI methods like source citation and chain-of-thought display to provide transparency into the tool's suggestions

To ensure GDPR compliance, we will utilize anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio and custom NER models to protect data when necessary. Our access control standards include multi-factor authentication enforcement with methods like TOTP and hardware tokens, role-based access control design experience, and privileged access management solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault.

For network security, we will follow zero-trust architecture patterns, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth, along with IDS/IPS deployment and annual plus post-major release penetration testing.

Our pricing model includes specific margins for infrastructure and software licence resale, which are 12 percent and 8 percent respectively. We estimate a total project cost of 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation that will remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority.

To limit the environmental footprint of the client's systems of information, we propose leveraging green hosting partners such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, who use 100% renewable energy. We will also implement digital sobriety practices like INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and adhering to a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle.

Our project management methodology is based on Agile Scrum, which allows for flexibility and adaptability throughout the project lifecycle. We will maintain a risk register, categorizing risks into standard categories such as Technical, Financial, Regulatory, Operational, and Reputational. Our governance tools, including RAID logs, decision logs, and escalation levels, will ensure that issues are properly documented and addressed in a timely manner.

# Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements from the tender have been left unaddressed.

# Conclusion
Our consortium proposes a comprehensive solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions. Our proposed solution leverages our expertise in LLMs, RAG, and explainability to provide a powerful intelligent assistance tool for administrative activities while ensuring GDPR compliance, sovereignty of data, and high availability. We believe that our solution will improve the efficiency of the municipal services and the quality of service rendered to the users, and we look forward to the opportunity to work with the City of Belval on this project.
